    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n103591" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τετρά̆-χορδος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			(<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χορδή</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>four-stringed</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὄργανον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ath.
					4.183a
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λύρα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Str.
					13.2.4
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			Subst.
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-χορδον, τό</span>, <i>tetrachord</i>, i.e. <i>scale of four
				notes</i>, comprising two tones and a half, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Pr.</u>
				922b8
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Fr.</u>
				47
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				2.1021e
			</span></i>, etc.: metaph., (sc. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">παθῶν</span>) <i><span class="en">
				Aristo Stoic.
				1.85
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Jul.
				<u>Caes.</u>
				315c
			</span></i>.</div>
